            <h2>Personal Profile</h2>
            <p>Welcome to my digital wellbeing website project. My name is Barry, and I am a Year 11 student studying at Sacred Heart College in Auckland, New Zealand. This website explores the complex relationship between modern youth, social media algorithms, and mental health in Aotearoa.</p>
            <p>In today's hyper-connected society, navigating digital spaces requires intentionality and balance. This project investigates how screen time, algorithmic design, and online communication impact adolescent development, backed by rigorous New Zealand research and ethical frameworks.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
            <h2>Catholic Perspective: Pope Francis on the Digital World</h2>
            <p>As part of our reflection on modern technology, we look to the teachings of Pope Francis. In his apostolic exhortation <em>Christus Vivit</em>, Pope Francis addresses young people directly regarding the digital environment:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>He warns that the digital world can become an environment of "loneliness, manipulation, exploitation, and violence".</li>
                <li>He cautions youth not to confuse genuine, authentic human communication with "mere virtual contact".</li>
                <li>In his broader teachings, he warns against becoming "couch potatoes" who let algorithms and corporations dictate our futures, urging us instead to build real-world connections and active communities.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>These teachings inspire me to examine how we can use digital tools as instruments for good without letting them replace face-to-face human relationships.</p>

